<article class="env-proposition" id="47329B">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/47329B">Proposition <span data-tag="47329B">5.3.5.10</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ and $\calD $ be $\infty $-categories, and let $\kappa $ be a regular cardinal. Suppose that $\calC $ is small and that $\calD $ admits small $\kappa $-filtered colimits. Then composition with the Yoneda embedding induces an equivalence of $\infty $-categories </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \bHom _{\kappa }( \Ind _{\kappa }(\calC ), \calD ) \rightarrow \Fun (\calC , \calD ), \]
</div>
  <p> where the left hand side denotes the $\infty $-category of all $\kappa $-continuous functors from $\Ind _{\kappa }(\calC )$ to $\calD $. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Lemma <a href="/tag/F8496B" data-tag="F8496B">5.3.5.8</a> with Corollary <a href="/tag/6C3CF8" data-tag="6C3CF8">4.3.2.16</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>